WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.630
The battle against Thanos is nearing its end.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:08.290
If you're a Marvel fan, you already know the
god of thunder is important, but here's a

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:14.119
look at some of the biggest reasons Thor will
be even more important in Avengers 4 than

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.480
you might already think.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.260
It's personal

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.560
Thor has really been through the ringer lately
between Thor: Ragnarok and Avengers: Infinity

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.060
War.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.680
After losing his father in Thor: Ragnarok,
he had to watch his brother be strangled to

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.680
death by Thanos right in front of his face
while he watched helplessly.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.240
And that was after watching his best friend
Heimdall get stabbed by Thanos too.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.800
Thor doesn't really have anyone left at this
point.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.360
"Your sister and your dad?"

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.220
"Both dead."

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.840
"But still got a mom, though?"

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.780
"Killed by a dark elf."

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:47.920
"Best friend?"

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.960
"Stabbed through the heart."

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.620
It's not the kind of thing you can just shake
off.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.180
You can bet Thor will remember that come Avengers
4.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.580
"I'm not sad, you idiot.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:58.780
I'm pissed off!"

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.700
"Ohhh."

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.820
"Angry!"

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.940
It's political

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.080
While Thor is clearly being eaten up by the
loss of his brother and friend, the other

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.110
glaring emotional factor at play here is his
role as the king of Asgard.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.520
Of course, the physical kingdom of Asgard
doesn't exist since Surtur destroyed it at

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.700
the end of Ragnarok.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.600
But the people of Asgard were still alive
and well, led by their fearless king and headed

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.050
for a new home, Earth, until they ran into
Thanos' ship and were partly slaughtered in

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:39.840
the process.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.640
Since Odin passed, Thor has had a pretty rough
go of it as King of Asgard.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.460
With the last of his people scattered and
homeless, adrift in space, Avengers 4 will

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.740
serve as the perfect chance for their king
to rise up.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.460
It's professional

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.860
While most of the Avengers found their way
into the superhero game, Thor was born into

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.360
it.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.880
He's been a hero and champion for thousands
of years and one of the original Avengers.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:09.509
When the dust settled at the end of Infinity
War, there were five very important characters

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.970
left: Iron Man, Captain America, Thor, Hulk,
and Black Widow.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:19.490
They're the original Avengers, and in Avengers
4, they're headed for an epic showdown with

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.200
Thanos.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:26.240
You can bet Thor will show up for work, and
not just as an angry god consumed with rage,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.080
but as a part of a well-oiled Avengers team.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.960
Frequent flyer

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.380
Thor is an intergalactic traveler who's very
comfortable with the perils of traveling through

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:36.880
space.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.660
This makes him a crucial element even in the
struggle to reach Thanos in the first place.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:46.690
It looks like Thanos is not on Earth as the
movie ends, and after that dreaded finger

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:51.000
snap, there just aren't that many intergalactic
superheroes left.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.830
Iron Man and Nebula are stranded on Titan,
and they'll likely need some space travel

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.060
in order to reconnect with everyone else.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.980
Rocket is still alive and an experienced pilot
to boot, but he didn't bring his spaceship

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.500
to Earth.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.720
Thor's role as a flying god who can summon
the Bifrost will definitely come in handy.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.300
Thor and Hulk: Besties

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.820
Thor and Hulk have been matched up throughout
the MCU saga in an endlessly entertaining,

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.120
rough and tumble relationship all along.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.440
From smashing around a giant aircraft in the
first Avengers movie to dueling in front of

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:30.300
a massive crowd gladiator style in Thor: Ragnarok,
the two Avengers are two of a kind.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.560
"We're the same, you and I.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.100
We're just a couple of hot-headed fools."

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:34.960
"Yeah, same.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.920
Hulk like fire, Thor like water."

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.260
But when push comes to shove, these two brawny
characters always come together to provide

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.500
some serious muscle to the Avengers team.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.739
With Hulk clearly shaping up to be an important
part of Avengers 4, there's no doubt that

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.440
Thor will be right there next to his friend
on the front lines.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.000
Trading up to Stormbreaker?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.800
We all loved Thor's hammer-wielding in the
past, and saying farewell to Mjolnir in Thor:

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:05.640
Ragnarok was a sad moment.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.840
"Sounds like you had a pretty special and
intimate relationship with this hammer and

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.700
that losing it was almost comparable to losing
a loved one."

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:13.720
"It's a nice way of putting it."

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:19.120
But the truth is that there's just as much
possibility in Thor's new weapon, if not more.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:23.540
When Thor arrived at the battle of Wakanda,
he used Stormbreaker to cut right through

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:28.480
the Infinity Gauntlet's power, showing that
his new axe was for more than chopping firewood.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.360
But we only got to see it in action in the
last few minutes of the movie, and Marvel

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:38.810
has proven over the years that they generally
don't build up huge plot momentum only to

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:41.340
fritter it away in a few moments.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.600
Stormbreaker aside, the hand wielding the
weapon has become even stronger.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.020
In a one on one fight, no one else can seem
to get a step up on Thanos, not even the Hulk.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.140
However, Thor actually managed to nearly kill
Thanos.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.740
His only mistake?

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.040
"You should've gone for the head."

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.640
Thor's story arc

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.800
Finally, we have Thor's story arc.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.820
While the god has been an established presence
in the MCU since he flew into theaters in

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:19.140
2011, we're really dealing with a whole new
character since Thor: Ragnarok.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.580
Before Ragnarok, Thor was little more than
a support character.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:28.320
After it, he became the bona fide king of
Asgard, and truly a top-tier character in

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.200
the MCU.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.700
With the third Avengers movie now on the books
and Avengers 4 heading toward its May 2019

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.840
release date, we can only wait and see how
Thor's character arc ends up.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.040
"I'm not as strong as you."

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.220
"No.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:47.720
You're stronger."

